title: AI-ku_superprogrammer
type: dataset
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
authors:
  - alias: Tito-Gl1tch3r
version: 0.9.0
date-released: "2026-10-11"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tito-Gl1tch3r/AI-ku_superprogrammer"
abstract: >-
  A fully synthetic, execution-verified training curriculum for code-generating
  LLMs. 24,525 records across 102 families and six datasets: code comprehension
  and writing (14 languages), generative TypeScript video (Three.js/Remotion
  style, deterministic renders), games and modding mixes, reverse engineering
  on real ELF binaries, and agent persistence over real long-running jobs.
  Every record passes GENERAR -> EJECUTAR -> COMPROBAR -> FILTRAR -> CONSERVAR:
  code is really compiled and executed in the sandbox, ground truth is measured
  (never asserted), adversarial duplicates are filtered, and anything not
  verified is quarantined. Splits are contamination-safe with an expert
  hard_holdout. MIT licensed; no third-party copyrighted content.
keywords:
  - synthetic-data
  - dataset
  - llm-training
  - code-generation
  - program-synthesis
  - reverse-engineering
  - typescript
  - agent-persistence
